  "answer_text": "Here is how you can log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd17 My Service Canada Account (MSCA) Login\n\n**Direct Login Link:**\n\ud83d\udc49 [https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)\n\n---\n\n## Sign-In Options\n\nThere are several ways to sign in to your MSCA:\n\n1. **GCKey**\nGCKey allows you to access multiple Government of Canada online services. You can use your GCKey username and password to log in.\n\n2. **Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner (Online Banking)**\nInterac\u00ae Sign-In Partner allows you to register or sign in using your online banking sign-in information to access MSCA.\n\n3. **Provincial Sign-In**\nYou can access My Service Canada Account (MSCA) by signing in or registering with your provincial sign-in. This service is currently only available for residents of Alberta and British Columbia.\n\n---\n\n## Need to Register?\n\nIf you don't have an account yet, you can create one at:\n\ud83d\udc49 [https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account/registration.html](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account/registration.html)\n\nBy clicking \"Start your registration,\" you will be able to create a GCKey username and password if you don't already have one. To create an account, you need to apply for a Social Insurance Number (SIN).\n\n---\n\n## Need Help?\n\n- **Forgot GCKey credentials?** Visit the [GCKey Help Page](https://www.canada.ca/en/government/sign-in-online-account.html)\n- **Personal Access Code (PAC)?** PACs are used to verify your identity when registering for MSCA. If you already applied for CPP/OAS benefits, your PAC has been sent to you by mail.\n- **Phone:** Call Service Canada at **1-800-206-7218**",
